.TH SPACEGL-SERVER 1 "2026-11-01" "SpaceGL @VERSION@" "SpaceGL Manual"
.SH NAME
spacegl-server \- SpaceGL galaxy server launcher script
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spacegl-server
.RB [ \-\-no\-banner ]
.RI [ "SERVER OPTIONS" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B spacegl-server
starts
.BR spacegl_server (1):
it shows the SpaceGL banner (on a terminal), makes sure a master key is
available, then replaces itself with the server. Every argument except
.B \-\-no\-banner
is passed on unchanged; the exit status and the signals are the
server's own.
.PP
On its first boot the server creates its own identity key,
.IR [DATA\-DIR]/server_identity.key ,
and prints its fingerprint ("Server identity CREATED ... SHA256:...");
on every later boot it prints "Server identity loaded". The decks pin
this identity (wire revision 4): back the file up together with the data
directory, or every deck that has met the server will refuse it as a
changed server.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-banner
No banner and no screen clearing.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
The script's usage, then the server's.
.PP
Every other option is the server's (see
.BR spacegl_server (1)),
in particular:
.TP
.B \-\-data\-dir DIR
Root directory of the persistent state (galaxy.dat, captains/,
server_identity.key).
.TP
.B \-\-print\-identity
Print the server's fingerprint and the 64 hex digits of its public key
(for
.B SPACEGL_SERVER_KEY
on the decks) and exit; needs no master key.
.TP
.B \-\-io=MODE
.B legacy
(default) or
.B async
event loop.
.SH MASTER KEY
The key is taken from the first source that exists:
.B SPACEGL_KEY_FILE
(a file of 64 hex digits, mode 0600),
.BR SPACEGL_KEY ,
.IR ~/.spacegl/key ;
the script names the source it found and the program reads it. Only when
none exists, and only on a terminal, the script asks for the key (not
echoed; 64 hex digits or at least 32 characters, three attempts) and
passes it in
.BR SPACEGL_KEY .
Without a terminal (a pipe, a service) nothing is asked and the program
creates
.IR ~/.spacegl/key .
.B \-\-help ,
.B \-\-version
and
.B \-\-print\-identity
show no banner and ask nothing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR SPACEGL_KEY_FILE ", " SPACEGL_KEY
The master key (see MASTER KEY).
.TP
.B SPACEGL_BIN_DIR
Directory of the program to run. Without it the script looks in the
build tree next to itself, in its own directory (an installed
.IR /usr/bin ),
in
.I ./build
and
.I .
of the current directory, then in
.BR PATH .
.TP
.B SPACEGL_NO_BANNER
1: no banner and no screen clearing (like
.BR \-\-no\-banner ).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Set: no colours (they are also off when the output is not a terminal).
.PP
For a server started at boot by systemd instead (optional, never enabled
by itself), see SYSTEM SERVICE in
.BR spacegl_server (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
The program's own (the script replaces itself with it);
.B 2
when no valid key was entered,
.B 127
when the program is not found.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I [DATA\-DIR]/server_identity.key
The server's identity (private key, mode 0600).
.TP
.I ~/.spacegl/key
The default master key.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
export SPACEGL_KEY_FILE=/etc/spacegl/master.key
spacegl\-server \-\-data\-dir /var/lib/spacegl
spacegl\-server \-\-data\-dir /var/lib/spacegl \-\-print\-identity
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR spacegl_server (1),
.BR spacegl-client (1),
.BR spacegl-diag (1)
